# qkt minimal project

This project was generated by `qkt create template --kind minimal`.

It starts a QKT daemon without a broker. Use it for local strategy development,
paper-only flows, and as the smallest base for adding your own broker wiring.

## First Run

```bash
cp .env.example .env
docker compose --env-file .env config --quiet
make up
make status
```

## Environment Values

Required:

- `QKT_IMAGE_TAG`: QKT image tag. The generated default pins to the QKT version
  that created this project.

Optional:

- `QKT_STARTING_BALANCE`: starting balance used by local config defaults.

Keep `.env` out of Git.

## Commands

- `make up`: start the QKT daemon.
- `make down`: stop containers without deleting state.
- `make restart`: restart QKT.
- `make logs`: tail daemon logs.
- `make status`: show deployed strategies.
- `make deploy STRAT=<name>`: deploy `/strategies/<name>.qkt` as `<name>`.
- `make resync-dry-run STRAT=<name>`: validate replacement without changing the running strategy.
- `make resync STRAT=<name>`: replace only that running deployment.
- `make reconcile STRAT=<name>`: compare QKT ledger to configured account state.
- `make stop STRAT=<name>`: stop one deployment.

## Strategy Flow

1. Edit or add a `.qkt` file in `strategies/`.
2. Run `make up`.
3. Deploy with `make deploy STRAT=<name>`.
4. For edits, run `make resync-dry-run`, then `make resync`, then `make reconcile`.

This scaffold has no live broker route by default.

